216},"Valentina Mignosa","#VM",[218,221,225],{"_":212,"xml:id":219,"ref":220},"JP","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537",{"_":222,"xml:id":223,"ref":224},"Simona Stoyanova","SS","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3914-9569",{"_":215,"xml:id":226,"ref":227},"VM","https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511",{"_":229,"when":230,"who":216},"Creation of file and EpiDoc encoding from published sources","2026-07-30",[232,235],{"atLeast":233,"atMost":234},25,35,{"atLeast":236,"atMost":237},7,8,[239,240,241,242,243,244,245],"Supplementum epigraphicum graecum, 1923-","Daux, 1937","Bousquet, 1964, Inscriptions de Delphes","De Waele, 1971, Acragas Graeca: die historische Topographie des griechischen Akragas auf Sizilien. 1, Historischer Teil","Jeffery, Johnston, 1990, LSAG","Dubois, 1989, IGDS","Arena, 2002, IGASMG II²",[247,248,249,250,251,252,253],"F2GG87EQ","BWAWZMS3","VB5QSXQK","CXHAXNBQ","QUWGZA84","RWXNUFEX","65P7AM6N",[255,256,257,21,26,30,258,259,260,261,262,263,264,119],"isic004485","dedication by an akragantine at delphi",{"_":5},"agrigentum","agrigento","sicilia","phocis","delphi","archaeological museum of delphi","ancient greek",[],{"title":267,"body":268,"divs":269,"editions":291,"images":301,"handnote":302},"ISic004485. Dedication by an Akragantine at Delphi","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]Ι̣ΟΣ \u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\">(vac.)\u003C/span> Ι̣ΑΙ̣ \u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\">(vac.)\u003C/span> [\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]Λ̣Σ̣Ι̣Λ̣ \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>\u003Ca href=\"http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462086\" target=\"_blank\">Ἀκρ]α̣γαντῖνος\u003C/a>. \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>].ΟΣ&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;.Α.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]....\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>\u003Ca href=\"http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462086\" target=\"_blank\">...].ΓΑΝΤΙΝΟΣ\u003C/a>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>  \u003Cspan>Text after Arena 2002 (IGASMG II² 93).\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 1\">line.1: \u003Cspan>Daux 1937 tentatively interpreted the surviving traces as the end of a personal name in \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">-ιος\u003C/span> or \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">-ος\u003C/span>, followed perhaps by the patronymic \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Μνασία\u003C/span>.\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>[— — —], an Akragantine.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The ethnic Ἀκραγαντῖνος is the only securely interpretable element. Daux regarded the text as a dedication rather than an artist's signature and attributed the form of gamma to an Akragantine stonecutter. Bousquet interpreted the holes on the upper bed as settings for at least two bronze statues and at least two stelae, suggesting an elongated base carrying a multi-figure dedication.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Daux 1937 60–61, pl. VII \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Bousquet 1959 150, n. 2 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001375\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001375\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> 1962 18.0210 \u003C/li>\u003Cli> De Waele 1971 40 no. 9 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002040\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002040\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Dubois 1989 \u003Ca href=\"http://www.persee.fr/doc/efr_0000-0000_1989_cat_119_1\" target=\"_blank\">182b\u003C/a>  \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000187\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000187\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Jeffery and Johnston 1990 278 no. 64 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000678\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000678\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Arena 2002 93 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001373\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001373\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\"> \u003Cp>Daux attributed the lettering to an Akragantine stonecutter on the basis of the form of gamma.\u003C/p> Lines 1–2  25–35  Interlineation  7–8  \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[270,273,276,279,282,285,288],{"id":271,"html":272},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003